<title>UK: Simon Group Aussie JV wins A$18 mln deal.</title>
<headline>Simon Group Aussie JV wins A$18 mln deal.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>British environmental and process engineering group Simon Group Plc said on Monday that a joint venture of its Australian subsidiary, Simon-Carves Australia had been awarded an A$18 ($13.34) million contract in the Australian state of Victoria.</p>
<p>Simon-Carves-Ahlstrom's contract involves mechanical and piping installation of a paper machine at Australian Paper's Maryvale Mill in the Latrobe Valley.</p>
<p>Australian Paper is the pulp and paper manufacturing business of Amcor Ltd.</p>
